            <ArticleTitle>Painful tonic seizures in multiple sclerosis: localization of a lesion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>359-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The history of a patient with painful tonic seizures in association with multiple sclerosis is related. These seizures have been thought by most authors to be spinal in origin. This case is reported because of the localization of a supratentorial lesion, clinically and on CT scan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
